        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Hdbm (0.945 mmol) and BuOK (1.399 mmol) were dissolved in methanol (6 mL). A solution of LnCl3·6H2O (0.477 mmol; Ln = Yb) in methanol (6 mL) was added. The mixture was stirred overnight, the solvent was distilled off under reduced pressure, and the residue was extracted with methylene chloride (10 mL). After centrifugation to remove solids, n-hexane (20 mL) was added. The precipitate was collected and dried; an additional portion was obtained by evaporating the mother liquor to 15 mL. Crystals of 1 were obtained from CH2Cl2–n-hexane.",
